 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool `input` against the tool's declared JSON Schema `inputSchema`
+  (using `ajv`) before calling the executor, enforcing `required`, declared property types and `enum` while
+  passing undeclared extra properties through unchanged without type coercion or default injection. When
+  validation fails, `execute` returns a `ToolResponse` (`{result}`) naming the failing property paths and
+  constraints — never the offending values — so the orchestrator feeds the rejection back to the model as a
+  `tool_result` within `maxToolRounds` instead of aborting the turn. Static tool schemas are compiled once at
+  `ToolRegistry.register` time (throwing synchronously if the schema cannot be compiled), and schemas from
+  function-valued tool definitions are compiled on execution and cached by schema object reference.
+
